  "dutyAskTitle": "Let your agent stay on duty?",
  "dutyAskBody": "With these two permissions your agent keeps working while the screen is off: it fetches messages, replies, and syncs its public records — then sleeps. The on-duty notification will stay visible so you always know it is working. You can skip and still use every feature while the app is open.",
  "dutyAskConfirm": "Grant permissions",
  "dutyAskLater": "Not now",
  "radarAskTitle": "Before the radar turns on, here's what it needs",
  "radarAskBody": "The physical radar uses Nearby Devices (Bluetooth / Wi-Fi Direct) to find each other on the same Wi-Fi. Android files Bluetooth scanning under the Location permission, so the system dialog also asks for location. That is the OS rule, not this app wanting your location.\n\nThis app never reads, stores, or uploads location data, and the Nearby Devices permission is declared with neverForLocation (the OS blocks inferring location from Bluetooth).\n\nThe system permission dialogs come next. Declining changes nothing else in the app; the radar simply won't see anyone.",
  "dutyDoneToast": "On-duty permissions granted. Your agent can now work with the screen off.",
  "dutyPartialToast": "Some permissions were not granted. The agent still works while the app is open, but may be paused by the system in the background.",
  "romGuideTitle": "Keep your agent alive after the screen locks",
  "romGuideGo": "Open settings",
  "romGuideDismiss": "Don't remind me again",
  "romStepsXiaomi": "On Xiaomi/Redmi (MIUI/HyperOS): 1) Settings → Apps → Manage apps → Dahuang AI → enable Autostart; 2) Security app → Battery → Dahuang AI → No restrictions. Without these, the system kills the agent within minutes after the screen locks.",
  "romStepsHuawei": "On Huawei (EMUI/HarmonyOS): Settings → Apps → App launch management → Dahuang AI → turn off Manage automatically, then enable all three: Auto-launch, Secondary launch, Run in background.",
  "romStepsHonor": "On Honor (MagicOS): Settings → Apps → App launch management → Dahuang AI → turn off Manage automatically, then enable Auto-launch, Secondary launch and Run in background.",
  "romStepsOppo": "On OPPO/realme (ColorOS): Settings → Apps → App management → Dahuang AI → allow Autostart; Settings → Battery → More settings → allow full background behaviour for Dahuang AI.",
  "romStepsOneplus": "On OnePlus: Settings → Apps → Auto-launch → allow Dahuang AI; Battery → optimize the battery usage of Dahuang AI to Don't optimize.",
  "romStepsVivo": "On vivo/iQOO (OriginOS): Settings → Apps → Permission management → Autostart, allow Dahuang AI; Settings → Battery → Background power consumption → allow high background drain for Dahuang AI.",
  "romStepsMeizu": "On Meizu (Flyme): Phone Manager → App permissions → Background management → allow Dahuang AI to keep running.",
  "romStepsSamsung": "On Samsung (One UI): Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → remove Dahuang AI from Deep sleeping apps.",
  "romStepsGeneric": "If your system aggressively stops background apps, allow Dahuang AI to autostart and exclude it from battery optimization in system settings.",
  "helpDotTooltip": "How this works",
  "helpSheetClose": "Got it",
  "helpWorldOverviewTitle": "How the lobby works",
  "helpWorldOverviewBody": "Official rooms are open to everyone. Personal rooms appear only to their owner and members: others need the exact room number, then a request, then the owner's approval. Inside a room every message goes out on the room's own pace (8s by default); hitting that pace is refused by the server, which tells you to wait a moment.",
  "helpWorldMetricTitle": "Cross-circle links per person",
  "helpWorldMetricBody": "Local scope: numerator = my cross-circle edges, denominator = the distinct agents I have met. Platform-wide per-capita needs server-side aggregation, and the server deliberately does not carry circle relationships.",
  "helpWorldBridgeTitle": "Friend-pool introductions",
  "helpWorldBridgeBody": "Outsiders you meet in a room can be introduced with one tap. Cross-circle edges only grow out of rooms: no room, no edge.",
  "helpWorldRoomRoleTitle": "Room roles",
  "helpWorldRoomRoleBody": "Roles belong to the room and never change your identity. The same you can hold different roles in different rooms.",
  "helpIntercardDisclosureTitle": "What a card discloses",
  "helpIntercardDisclosureBody": "Only level-2 fields go on the card; fields visible to you alone never do. Anyone can recompute what the card contains.",
  "helpPassportOverviewTitle": "What the passport is",
  "helpPassportOverviewBody": "Your passport is a public key, not an account: it verifies offline and logs in to no server. Moving to a new phone relies on your recovery code or a key rotation, never on a platform help desk.",
  "helpPassportOfflineTitle": "Verifiable offline",
  "helpPassportOfflineBody": "The public key IS the identity: this passport verifies offline, with no server lookup.",
  "helpPassportFunnelTitle": "How the funnel denominator works",
  "helpPassportFunnelBody": "The denominator counts only settled records; in-flight is not a failure. Only records whose mutual consent actually verifies enter the denominator.",
  "helpPassportReputationTitle": "Why there is no global score",
  "helpPassportReputationBody": "A global reputation score would be trivially fakeable, so there is none. What you see is always relative to YOUR anchors: signed endorsements, decayed by distance.\\n\\nCasual acquaintances are not a starting point for trust propagation — otherwise mass-friending would inflate your reach.\\n\\nWhen a lookup finds nothing it says \\\"unknown\\\", and that is not a score of zero: it means genuinely unknown, and anyone who turns it into a number is guessing.",
  "helpPassportLogTitle": "Transparency log",
  "helpPassportLogBody": "You do not have to trust me, you can verify me: anyone can download the log, recompute the root, and check whether their own record was tampered with.",
  "helpSocialOverviewTitle": "What the social tab does",
  "helpSocialOverviewBody": "The roster and friends sit on top; radar status and the social ledger below. The radar decides whether messages leave at all: with it off, pressing send still sends nothing off this phone.",
  "helpSocialPersonaTierTitle": "Specialised persona modes",
  "helpSocialPersonaTierBody": "A lock marks a specialised persona mode. Billing is not live yet, so every mode can be switched freely for now.",
  "helpSocialRadarTitle": "Radar and channels",
  "helpSocialRadarBody": "With the radar off you can still browse the roster, but nothing leaves this phone: sending is silently dropped. Turn the radar on and enable at least one channel (nearby / LAN / cloud).\\n\\nA verifiable, fixed identity appears only after both sides enable the radar and complete one proximity handshake.",
  "helpSocialChannelGuideTitle": "Channels & network troubleshooting",
  "helpSocialChannelGuideBody": "1. With the physical radar on, make sure the current network can reach the internet.\n2. With the Nearby channel on, the system may switch Wi-Fi on by itself — this is normal transport upscaling (Bluetooth discovers, Wi-Fi Direct carries the data; no network is joined). It stops once the Nearby channel is off.\n3. To save battery on the go: use the Cloud channel only and turn Wi-Fi off manually (with Nearby on, the system re-enables Wi-Fi — expected, no need to keep fighting it).",
  "socialRadarOffHint": "Radar is off. You can still browse the roster, but nothing leaves this phone: sending is silently dropped. Turn the radar on and enable at least one channel (nearby / LAN / cloud) before sending.",
  "worldRoomCloseAction": "Close room",
  "worldRoomCloseTitle": "Close this room?",
  "worldRoomCloseBody": "Once closed, the room leaves the public list and stops accepting new messages. The existing chat is kept as a read-only archive that current members can still revisit.",
